    "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/jobs/career-programmes/finance-graduate-scheme-/finance/example-placements/management-reporting/": {
      "title": "Management Reporting",
      "description": "Management Reporting | Jobs | Imperial College London Skip to main content View accessibility support page Search Search Menu Study Research Faculties News Events About Get involved Giving Shop Imperial Search Search Website navigation Close Key links This section Skip to section navigation Global site navigation Study Course search Subjects Apply Fees and funding Student life Visit Help centre Request info International students Lifelong Learning Summer schools Research Faculties Faculty of Engineering Faculty of Medicine Faculty of Natural Sciences Imperial Business School Administrative and support services News News Imperial Stories Imperial Magazine Events What's on Great Exhibition Road Festival Imperial Lates Graduation About President Provost and Deputy President Council Imperial Strategy League tables and rankings Imperial Global Sustainable Imperial School of Convergence Science Governance Campuses Our academics Jobs at Imperial Get involved Giving Schools outreach Imperial Global Summer School Societal engagement Volunteering and outreach Women at Imperial Giving Shop Imperial User links navigation For staff Current students Imperial for business For schools Alumni Career programmes Finance Graduate Scheme navigation Graduate Finance Training Scheme About Apply Learning and development Example placements Financial Accounting Faculty offices Management Reporting Trainee profiles Ellie Andrew Ed Isabel Max Kavan Izzy Hiro Salary and benefits Person specification Frequently Asked Questions In this section Finance Graduate Scheme Finance Graduate Scheme Imperial Home Jobs Career programmes Finance Graduate Scheme Graduate Finance Training Scheme Example placements Management Reporting Management Reporting Example placements Financial Accounting Faculty offices Management Reporting Part of College’s Central Financial Management function, Management Reporting is responsible for the provision of financial analysis, advice and support to Faculties, Academic and Support Services. Key aspects of the team’s role include the preparation of management accounting reports and the formulation of budgets and financial plans for approval by the Provost’s Board and the College Council. Aspects of the placement role include: Managing the provision of financial information, analysis and advice to support the operational management of various Support and Academic service areas within College Preparation of monthly Finance Management Reports for selected support services, and for inclusion in the monthly report for review by Council and Management Board. Reports include detailed analysis of performance against budget, realistic full year forecast, key performance indicators, and commentaries presented in a form that aids management to understand and control College activities Assisting in the preparation of annual budget and quarterly forecasts for areas supported Ensuring compliance and accuracy of external funds finance within areas supported Useful Links Popular links Canvas Contact the Service Desk Jobs Library services Outlook email online Faculties Engineering Medicine Natural Sciences Imperial Business School Directories Admin and support services Networks and Centres Research groups Search all staff Partners Imperial College Academic Health Science Centre Imperial College Health Partners Imperial College Healthcare NHS Trust Imperial Consultants College Information Imperial College London Address Imperial College London South Kensington Campus London SW7 2AZ , UK tel: +44 (0)20 7589 5111 Facebook X, formerly known as Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Instagram TikTok Bluesky Site Information Sitemap Accessibility Modern slavery statement Privacy notice Use of cookies Report incorrect content Log in © 2026 Imperial College London We use cookies to maintain and analyse our website performance and for advertising purposes. Where cookies have been categorised as ‘strictly necessary’ they are required to keep the site work